+.. _cli_relational_merge:
+
+Merging related tables with fresh IDs
+====================================
+
+Use ``merge-preserving-keys`` to import independent integer ID spaces into existing
+destination tables:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils merge-preserving-keys combined.db \
+        --source north north.db --source south south.db \
+        --table people --table teams
+
+Each ``--source`` takes a persistent ID and SQLite file path. Repeat ``--table``
+to select a graph closed over outgoing foreign keys. The command allocates fresh
+integer primary keys, rewrites relationships and atomically records source
+identity and key maps. Successful output is the Python API's JSON result. Errors
+print ``Error:`` and exit nonzero without committing a partial merge.
+
+Run the command again with unchanged sources to retrieve saved maps without
+inserting duplicates. A moved file or checkpointed WAL is acceptable, while
+changed selected rows, definitions or table selection under an existing ID is an
+error. See :ref:`the Python API <python_api_relational_merge>` for supported key
+layouts, snapshot behavior and transaction ownership.
+
